 iELT  ^The iELT content was presented in two sessions, separated by 5 minutes, with the test first and the iELT as its follow-up. Each session was followed by a waiting period of five minutes. The participants were asked to respond in only 5 minutes, so, there was no way to recall the previous information, which led us to study only the first passage. Upon request, the iELT content was repeated during the follow-up phase.

